Do not delete: this patch changes source from SQLite3 Multiple Ciphers
(https://github.com/utelle/SQLite3MultipleCiphers), Copyright (c) 2019-2026
Ulrich Telle, MIT licence. NOTICE at the repository root contains the licence
text. The patch adds the SQL function sirannon_export(schema), which copies the
main database into an attached database inside the caller's open transaction.
It runs the copy steps of SQLite's VACUUM INTO, marked as VACUUM INTO so that
the transfer keeps every rowid of the source, and the codec of the attached
database encrypts each page that it writes, so a key change copies a snapshot
to a file under another key. The patch also adds sirannon_copy_codec, which
gives a backup's destination a copy of the source's cipher, so the key stays
inside SQLite3 Multiple Ciphers.

--- a/sqlite3.c
+++ b/sqlite3.c
